{"global_index": "OpenTDB_History_2185", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The coat of arms of the King of Spain contains the arms from the monarchs of Castille, Leon, Aragon and which other former Iberian kingdom?\n\nOptions: \nA. Catalonia\nB. Granada\nC. Galicia\nD. Navarre\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is B. Granada. The coat of arms of the King of Spain includes the arms of Castile, León, Aragon, and Granada, which represents the unification of the various kingdoms that formed modern Spain. Granada, in particular, symbolizes the last Muslim kingdom in the Iberian Peninsula, which was conquered by the Catholic Monarchs in 1492. \n\nThus, the answer is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 203}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is B. Granada. The coat of arms of the King of Spain includes the arms of Castile, León, Aragon, and Granada, which represents the unification of the various kingdoms that formed modern Spain. Granada, in particular, symbolizes the last Muslim kingdom in the Iberian Peninsula, which was conquered by the Catholic Monarchs in 1492. \n\nThus, the answer is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.005e-05}}
